al through commercial  manufacturing  there are two main ways  we provide safety and quality  dna sequencing and real-time pcr  technologies  specifically we provide high-throughput  highly specific analytical solutions for  microplasma detection  residual dna  and virus detection  with real-time pcr  and with our dna sequencing technology  we enable you to do microbial  identification  of bacterial and fungal organisms  due to the possible harmful effects of  microorganisms  regulatory agencies expect  pharmaceutical organizations to have an  environmental monitoring program as part  of good manufacturing practices  it is also recommended to identify  microorganisms at the species level  at frequent intervals  to establish a valid  current database of contaminants  present in a facility  after choosing the id technology to be  implemented the system needs to be  validated and verified  usp  1113 describes the recommendation  for verification of id method  specifically the usp monograph  recommended to include one of the  following tests  use an existing system to do  comparability tests of isolates from  routine testing  the number of isops can be as high as 50  or  testing  by the use of let's say 12 to 15  reference stock cultures of different  commonly isolated species  or  confirming  20 to 50 organisms  that get id'd which includes 50 to 20  species with a reference lab  it is important to note that the  parameters used to verify the methods  are accurate and reproducible  how the data records are maintained can  be based on four main characteristics  these include reliability  accuracy  usability  integrity  because data integrity is so important  what is data integrity  it is really comprised of several topics  first there is the focus on the accuracy  of data being generated and it  next  how the data is being recorded and  stored  and finally  data integrity should be managed and  processed  based on good documentation practices  now there are three main ways to achieve  compliant data integrity through csv  first  you can choose to work with a third  party consultant  but you will need to consider their  experience with regulatory requirements  and quality  second you may rely on internal company  resources but they may lack the  experience with the microseek id system  and finally you can rely on thermofisher  scientific to have the experience  of your microseek id system and  knowledge of regulatory concerns to  assist you with your validation  expand on this topic allow me to  introduce my colleague sandy true  she has many years of experience in the  field working with customers just like  you  and hearing about their challenges with  computer systems validation  for microbial identification  thanks daryl as you noted i've had many  years experience helping customers with  their computer system validation  as they implement environmental  monitoring for microbial pathogen  identification  as a staff scientist with our field  application group  it's my honor to assist customers in  this process  and what i'd like to do today is to go  through a couple examples of real world  experiences where customers have used  either third party  groups to help with their computer  system validation or they've used  internal resources to go through this  and to explain how both of these  situations have resulted in different  experiences for the customer and the  ways that thermo fisher has been able to  assist them in both  so what i'd like to start with here  is  the example of  a customer that i worked with in years  past that used a third party contractor  for their csv  in this situation the customer chose to  use a third-party contractor because  they had multiple sites across north  america where they were implementing  the csv at each of these sites  but in each of these cases the  contractor was in control of the  installation and access to the  microseekid system  and the contractor didn't have any  training on our system at all  so the users of the system were forced  to take training before the contractor  had finished their validation process  and then the system was not enabled and  not put into use before the validation  was complete  so the users were left without a system  that they could use but had been trained  on  now  when this happened the contractor set  out a number of worst case scenarios and  this is pretty typical in any  csv situation  they're looking to test the system to  make sure that they enable it to pass  any risk that might take place  so  this ended up resulting in software  conflicts and errors  because the contractor didn't know the  capabilities of our microseek id  software  and  this resulted in the contractor needing  to come back to thermo fisher in order  to seek resolution for these errors  so this resulted in  a lot of time and support being spent  not only on my  time but also on the part of our  engineering team to go in and to  actually repair some of the errors that  were taking place and were set up by the  use of the contractor setting out these  worst case scenarios  in the end  system validation took well over 18  months from the time the system was  installed until the time the actual  users could start using it for their  microbial identification  there were repeated software conflicts  and errors and these took long  resolution times because the contractor  tried to solve them themselves before  they came to me for support  then the users had to purchase an  additional training and this ended up  costing them time and money because they  had been trained too early in the  process  but the biggest cost then to the user  actually ended up being money that they  spent having to outsource testing  because it spent so long in the  validation process they actually weren't  able to get their system up and running  very quickly and they had to outsource  this environmental testing to others and  that cost them a lot of money  so this is 